Article 13 Under any of the following circumstances, a futures brokerage contract shall be determined void:
(1) engaging in futures brokerage business without the subject qualification for futures brokerage business;
(2) a client lacking the subject qualification for futures trading engages in futures trading;
(3) violating the mandatory provisions of laws and administrative regulations.

Article 22 Where a futures company erroneously executes a client's trading instruction, unless the client approves it, the consequences of the trading shall be borne by the futures company, and shall be handled separately in the following ways:
(1) if an error occurs in the transaction quantity, the portion exceeding the instructed quantity shall be borne by the futures company, and the portion less than the instructed quantity shall be supplemented by the futures company or compensated as direct losses;
(2) if the transaction price exceeds the range of the client's instructed price, the loss from the price difference or the trading result shall be borne by the futures company.
